\name{semantica_condition_info}\alias{semantica_condition_info}\title{Inspect a SEMANTICA condition programmatically}\usage{semantica_condition_info(condition)}\arguments{\item{condition}{An error, warning, or other condition object.}}\description{Returns the condition class, message, and structured metadata fields already attached by SEMANTICA when available. It does not change condition signaling.}\value{A named list suitable for scripted logging or recovery logic.}
